text "profiler.diagnosis.col_what" "क्या गलत है"
text "profiler.diagnosis.col_where" "कहाँ"
text "profiler.diagnosis.details" "विवरण"
text "profiler.diagnosis.empty" "No findings: the measured frames are inside their budgets."
text "profiler.diagnosis.from_measurements" "Findings come from the measurements of the last frames."
text "profiler.diagnosis.ignore" "अनदेखा करें"
text "profiler.diagnosis.ignored" "Ignored"
text "profiler.diagnosis.limit" "limit"
text "profiler.diagnosis.listed" "{count} findings listed"
text "profiler.diagnosis.measured" "measured"
text "profiler.diagnosis.nothing" "Nothing to fix"
text "profiler.diagnosis.pick" "Pick a finding to see why it hurts and what to do."
text "profiler.diagnosis.proof" "Proof from the measurement"
text "profiler.diagnosis.recoverable" "to win back ({percent}% of the frame) by fixing what was measured"
text "profiler.diagnosis.rules_note" "The diagnosis compares the measurements with the budgets of the counters. Change a budget in Counters and the findings follow."
text "profiler.diagnosis.severity" "गंभीरता"
text "profiler.diagnosis.show" "Show in measurements"
text "profiler.diagnosis.show_ignored" "अनदेखे दिखाएँ"
text "profiler.diagnosis.todo" "क्या करें"
text "profiler.diagnosis.why" "नुकसान क्यों"
text "profiler.finding.draw_calls_high.detail" "Every draw call costs the CPU time to prepare and submit. Many small objects with the same mesh and material can be drawn together."
text "profiler.finding.draw_calls_high.step1" "Merge meshes that share a material, or draw them as instances."
text "profiler.finding.draw_calls_high.step2" "Compare the Visible meshes counter with the draw calls: they should be close."
text "profiler.finding.draw_calls_high.title" "{value} draw calls a frame, over the {limit} threshold"
text "profiler.finding.frame_over_budget.frame" "Neither the graphics card nor the game thread explains it alone. Select the slowest frame in Measurements and read its hierarchy."
text "profiler.finding.frame_over_budget.game" "The game thread takes most of each frame. Look for the largest regions under Game tick in Measurements."
text "profiler.finding.frame_over_budget.gpu" "The graphics card takes most of each frame. Lower what it draws: fewer triangles, cheaper materials, smaller shadows."
text "profiler.finding.frame_over_budget.step1" "Open Measurements and select a frame over the budget."
text "profiler.finding.frame_over_budget.step2" "Read its hierarchy: the region with the most time of its own is the one to fix first."
text "profiler.finding.frame_over_budget.title" "The frame takes {value} ms, over the {limit} ms budget"
text "profiler.finding.frame_spikes.detail" "A few frames are far slower than their neighbours, which is felt as stutter."
text "profiler.finding.frame_spikes.step1" "Select a spike in the Frame chart and read what its hierarchy holds."
text "profiler.finding.frame_spikes.step2" "Look for loading, allocation or a script that runs only now and then."
text "profiler.finding.frame_spikes.title" "{value} frames cost more than {limit} ms"
text "profiler.finding.hot_region.detail" "This region holds more than {limit}% of its frame, and {gain} ms of that is its own work."
text "profiler.finding.hot_region.step1" "Select this frame in Measurements and open the region in the hierarchy."
text "profiler.finding.hot_region.step2" "Do less work in it, or do it less often."
text "profiler.finding.hot_region.title" "{subject} takes {value}% of the frame"
text "profiler.finding.memory_growth.detail" "Process memory keeps rising instead of settling. Something is created every frame and never released."
text "profiler.finding.memory_growth.step1" "Watch Process memory while the scene runs without changes."
text "profiler.finding.memory_growth.step2" "Look for objects, textures or buffers that are created in a loop."
text "profiler.finding.memory_growth.title" "Memory grew by {value} MB over {limit} frames"
text "profiler.finding.triangles_high.detail" "More triangles than the target can draw in time. The cost lands on the graphics card."
text "profiler.finding.triangles_high.step1" "Use simpler levels of detail for objects that are far away."
text "profiler.finding.triangles_high.step2" "Remove geometry the camera never sees."
text "profiler.finding.triangles_high.title" "{value} thousand triangles a frame, over the {limit} thousand threshold"
text "profiler.footer.note" "Changes take effect at once, in the profiler and on the scene."
